==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|VL.|*morīre}}, from {{inh|es|la|morī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|morior}}, ultimately from {{der|es|ine-pro|*mer-}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-IPA}}
* {{audio|es|LL-Q1321 (spa)-Rodelar-morir.wav|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb}}

# to [[die]]
#: {{syn|es|estirar la pata|fallecer|morirse|palmar|petatearse}}
#: {{ux|es|La caballerosidad no ha '''muerto'''.|Chivalry is not '''dead'''.}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to [[die]]
#: {{syn|es|morir}}

====Usage notes====
* The [[reflexive]] form for this verb is more [[colloquial]], while non-reflexive form ({{m|es|morir}}) is more formal.
* Widely used figuratively:
** {{uxi|es|Me morí del aburrimiento|lit=I died because of boredom|boredom was [[insufferable]] for me}}
** {{uxi|es|Me morí del susto|lit=I died because of [[fright]]|fright was [[terrible]] for me}}

